# Follow a Web Request

A long request path demonstrates LDOC's moving camera. It follows each stage and arrow downward, then zooms out to reveal the complete journey.

@animate
The browser creates an HTTPS request
DNS resolves the domain to an IP address
A TCP connection is established
The load balancer selects a healthy server
The API gateway authenticates the request
The application server runs business logic
The database returns the requested records
The server builds and sends the response
The browser renders the result
@end
